# A ring reef: n spots in a circle; each year every spot becomes
# (left + itself + right) mod 3. When does the reef repeat? echo knows.
# The reef lives in cells 1,000,001 and up; the next year is built in cells 2,000,001 and up.

: n 13 ;
: cell 1000000 + dig ;
: left dup 1 = if drop n else 1 - then ;
: right dup n = if drop 1 else 1 + then ;
: grow dup left cell over cell + over right cell + 3 % swap 2000000 + bury ;
: copy dup 2000000 + dig swap 1000000 + bury ;
: year 1 [ dup grow 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop
       1 [ dup copy 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop ;
: show 1 [ dup cell 46 35 rot 1 = if swap then drop emit 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop 10 emit ;
: listen 1000001 1000000 n + echo ;

1 n 2 / 1 + 1000000 + bury
0 -1 bury
# year by year, until echo hears a picture it has heard before
listen drop
1 [ drop show year -1 dig 1 + -1 bury listen dup 0 = ] drop
. ." is the cycle of the reef, in years. It first came back after " -1 dig . ." years"
